  "question": {
    "text": "Equilibrium constant K<sub>p</sub> for the reaction <math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CaCO</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <mo>⇌</mo><mtext>CaO</mtext><mo>+</mo><msub> <mrow> <mtext>CO</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> is 0.82 atm at <math> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> <mn>2</mn> <msup> <mn>7</mn> <mo>∘</mo> </msup> <mtext>C.</mtext> </mrow> </math><br />\rIf 1 mole of CaCO<sub>3</sub> is placed in a closed container of 20 L and heated to this temperature, what amount of CaCO<sub>3</sub> would dissociate at equilibrium?",
